<p>President Trump said at the White House on April 23 that the United States would not use a nuclear weapon in any war with Iran, saying, “A nuclear weapon should never be allowed to be used by anybody”. In the same exchange, he said Washington was “in no rush” but that “the clock is ticking” for Iran. The remarks came as a third US aircraft carrier arrived in the Middle East, adding a visible sign of military pressure even as Trump signaled no immediate move.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Bgz_XknrGWuMXGWrGSSi6OOCLBnM1ckTCE0DI718JLPWZuIopaBzhNARpCTn-aItoD-EeJ9k6d0YFrYscbtnCzVIdivYDm9udjiYYgyFwwLObu773U0IVs5VNCJNITGbeUNOfmZ69otvl1qUpiUy2P2lP1Gg__Q0lBocOJz5M0s9CsFuxA' alt='US President Donald Trump in the Oval Office of the White House in Washington, DC, on April 23, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Conventional emphasis: Trump said Iran had already been “decimated” through conventional means and asked why he would use a nuclear weapon, arguing that US military power was sufficient without crossing that threshold.</li><li>Public setting: Trump made the nuclear remark in exchanges with reporters at the White House, giving it the weight of an on-record presidential position rather than an off-camera briefing.</li><li>Regional buildup: The arrival of a third aircraft carrier added a visible sign of US force projection in the Middle East at the same moment Trump said Washington was not rushing its next move.</li></ul><blockquote>A nuclear weapon should never be allowed to be used by anybody. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: He said the United States would not use a nuclear weapon against Iran and argued that conventional operations had already inflicted severe damage, while also warning that time was running out for Tehran. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/trump-rules-out-striking-iran-nuclear-weapon'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Regional security coverage: Reports tied Trump’s 